                    ],
                    "Value": {
                      "StringWithMarkup": [
                        {
                          "String": "The Henry's Law constant for siduron is estimated as 6.8X10-11 atm-cu m/mole(SRC) derived from its vapor pressure, 4.0X10-9 mm Hg(1), and water solubility, 18 mg/L(2). This Henry's Law constant indicates that siduron is expected to be essentially nonvolatile from water(3) and moist soil surfaces(SRC). Siduron is not expected to volatilize from dry soil surfaces(SRC) based upon its vapor pressure of 4.0X10-9 mm Hg(1).",
