        "Description": "SangsterLogP is the largest publicly available curated dataset of experimental logP values. It originates from Dr. James Sangster's literature review of 3,000 books and articles. It is processed via logD-to-logP adjustments for ionized compounds and consensus-based residual analysis to remove duplicates and outliers. It is predominantly Rule-of-5 (Ro5) compliant (96.5%), but also expands into beyond-Rule-of-5 (bRo5) chemical space (macrocycles, peptides, and protein degraders).",
